response:
**Gates before launch.** I run these in order, and any failure stops the launch. First I confirm that spe/predictions/r04.yaml and spe/plans/r04.md are in the last commit and unchanged since then. Gate 1 is the grader selftest. grade.py must pass the oracle (answers.json fed back as predictions) on all 50 tickets. It must fail an empty predictions file and a file where every category and priority is set to a wrong value. This gate also checks that answers.json holds 50 tickets, because the original eval set had 40 and the plan needs 50. Gate 2 is the control. I regrade round 3's saved outputs with this round's grade.py and compare them to round 3's recorded scores. Any change means the grader changed, and I report it before launch. Gate 3 is a dry run with args.only set to one B cell and one C2 cell, trials 2, and spendCapUsd 3. It must return schema-valid trials, grades, and judge scores, and no paths_read entry may sit under spe/evals/ or spe/predictions/. The costs it measures become estTrialUsd, estAgentUsd, and estJudgeUsd for the real run. Then I save the script as spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js, commit it locally as "spe r04: eval harness", and launch it with round 4, the 50 label-free tickets, and spendCapUsd 40. Nothing gets pushed.

Assumptions: the triage runner is `node triage/cli.js --config <file> --ticket <file> --json`, the configs are triage/configs/B.yaml and triage/configs/C2.yaml, and grade.py accepts `--answers --preds --json`. If any of these differ, change `runCmd`, `configs`, or the grade command line.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage agent. Trials per config and ticket, code grade on labels, Opus judge on reply tone, top-up of mixed cells, failure analysis, and a completeness critic.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Top-up' },
    { title: 'Synthesis' },
  ],
};

// Arguments. All paths and prompt text derive from args.round.
//   round          SPE round number. Required.
//   tasks          [{id, text}] ticket ids and text. Labels are not allowed here.
//   expectTasks    task count a full run must have. Default 50.
//   configs        {name: config file}. Default B and C2.
//   runCmd         command that runs one triage trial and prints one JSON object.
//   trials         trials per cell. Default 5.
//   topupPerCell   extra trials for a cell with mixed results. Default 5.
//   topupMaxCells  most cells that get a top-up. Default 30.
//   spendCapUsd    hard cap for the whole run. Default 40.
//   estTrialUsd    cost of one triage trial, measured in the dry run.
//   estAgentUsd    cost of one driver or grader agent call, measured in the dry run.
//   estJudgeUsd    cost of one Opus judge or synthesis call, measured in the dry run.
//   only           cell keys such as "B:T-1042" for a dry run.

const a = args ?? {};
const ROUND = Number(a.round);
if (!Number.isInteger(ROUND) || ROUND < 1) throw new Error('args.round is required');
const RR = `r${String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')}`;
const OUT = `spe/evals/results/${RR}`;
const PREDICTIONS = `spe/predictions/${RR}.yaml`;
const GRADER = 'spe/evals/graders/grade.py';
const ANSWERS = 'spe/evals/tasks/answers.json';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';
const FORBIDDEN = ['spe/evals/', 'spe/predictions/', 'spe/plans/'];

const CONFIGS = a.configs ?? { B: 'triage/configs/B.yaml', C2: 'triage/configs/C2.yaml' };
const RUN_CMD = a.runCmd ?? 'node triage/cli.js';
const TRIALS = a.trials ?? 5;
const TOPUP_PER_CELL = a.topupPerCell ?? 5;
const TOPUP_MAX_CELLS = a.topupMaxCells ?? 30;
const CAP = a.spendCapUsd ?? 40;
const ONLY = Array.isArray(a.only) && a.only.length > 0 ? new Set(a.only) : null;
const HARNESS_MODEL = 'opus';
const JUDGE_MODEL = 'opus';
const JUDGE_NOTE = 'The tone judge is Opus. No judge from another model family is available in this harness, so the judge and the trial model share Claude blind spots.';

for (const k of ['estTrialUsd', 'estAgentUsd', 'estJudgeUsd']) {
  if (!(typeof a[k] === 'number' && a[k] > 0)) {
    throw new Error(`args.${k} is required. Use the dry run measurement, or a rough guess for the dry run itself.`);
  }
}
const EST_TRIAL = a.estTrialUsd;
const EST_AGENT = a.estAgentUsd;
const EST_JUDGE = a.estJudgeUsd;

const TASKS = a.tasks;
if (!Array.isArray(TASKS) || TASKS.length === 0) throw new Error('args.tasks is required');
for (const t of TASKS) {
  const extra = Object.keys(t).filter((k) => k !== 'id' && k !== 'text');
  if (extra.length > 0) throw new Error(`HALT: task ${t.id} carries ${extra.join(', ')}. Labels must not reach trials.`);
}
const EXPECT = a.expectTasks ?? 50;
if (!ONLY && TASKS.length !== EXPECT) throw new Error(`HALT: ${TASKS.length} tasks given, the plan needs ${EXPECT}`);

const range = (start, count) => Array.from({ length: count }, (_, i) => start + i);
const isNum = (x) => typeof x === 'number' && Number.isFinite(x);
const round2 = (x) => Math.round(x * 100) / 100;
const round3 = (x) => Math.round(x * 1000) / 1000;
const mean = (xs) => {
  const v = xs.filter(isNum);
  return v.length ? round3(v.reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0) / v.length) : null;
};
const sum = (xs) => xs.filter(isNum).reduce((s, x) => s + x, 0);

// ---- Budget ----
let spent = 0;
const skipped = [];
function reserve(usd, what) {
  if (spent + usd > CAP) {
    skipped.push({ what, reason: 'spend cap', need_usd: round2(usd), spent_usd: round2(spent) });
    log(`SKIP ${what}: $${round2(spent)} spent, $${round2(usd)} more would cross the $${CAP} cap`);
    return false;
  }
  spent += usd;
  return true;
}
function settle(reserved, actual) {
  spent += actual - reserved;
}

// ---- Halt ----
let HALT = null;
function halt(reason) {
  if (!HALT) {
    HALT = reason;
    log(`HALT: ${reason}`);
  }
}

// ---- Cells ----
const cells = [];
for (const cfg of Object.keys(CONFIGS)) {
  for (const task of TASKS) {
    const key = `${cfg}:${task.id}`;
    if (!ONLY || ONLY.has(key)) cells.push({ key, cfg, task, trials: [], grades: [], judgments: [] });
  }
}
if (ONLY && cells.length !== ONLY.size) throw new Error(`args.only names ${ONLY.size} cells but ${cells.length} match`);
log(`${RR}: ${cells.length} cells, ${TRIALS} trials each, configs ${Object.keys(CONFIGS).join(', ')}, cap $${CAP}`);

// ---- Schemas ----
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['trials'],
  properties: {
    trials: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['n', 'status', 'paths_read'],
        properties: {
          n: { type: 'integer' },
          status: { type: 'string', enum: ['completed', 'harness_error', 'rate_limited'] },
          error: { type: 'string' },
          label: {
            type: 'object',
            properties: { category: { type: 'string' }, priority: { type: 'string' } },
          },
          reply: { type: 'string' },
          metrics: {
            type: 'object',
            required: ['runtime_s', 'tool_calls', 'tool_errors', 'input_tokens', 'output_tokens', 'cost_usd'],
            properties: {
              runtime_s: { type: 'number' },
              tool_calls: { type: 'integer' },
              tool_errors: { type: 'integer' },
              input_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
              output_tokens: { type: 'integer' },
              cost_usd: { type: 'number' },
            },
          },
          paths_read: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['grades'],
  properties: {
    grader_error: { type: 'string' },
    grades: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['n', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: {
          n: { type: 'integer' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scores'],
  properties: {
    scores: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['reply', 'score', 'pass', 'reason'],
        properties: {
          reply: { type: 'integer' },
          score: { type: 'number' },
          pass: { type: 'boolean' },
          reason: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
};

const ANALYSIS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['verdicts', 'failures', 'proposals'],
  properties: {
    verdicts: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['metric', 'config', 'predicted', 'measured', 'verdict'],
        properties: {
          metric: { type: 'string' },
          config: { type: 'string' },
          predicted: { type: 'string' },
          measured: { type: ['number', 'null'] },
          verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['hit', 'miss', 'not_scorable'] },
          note: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
    failures: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['id', 'summary', 'evidence'],
        properties: { id: { type: 'string' }, summary: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
    proposals: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['change', 'source'],
        properties: { change: { type: 'string' }, source: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: 'boolean' },
    gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
};

// ---- Prompts ----
function trialPrompt(cell, ns) {
  const cfgFile = CONFIGS[cell.cfg];
  const ticketFile = `/tmp/triage-${RR}/${cell.task.id}.txt`;
  return `You drive the triage eval harness. You run the triage agent and report what it printed. You do not triage the ticket yourself, and you do not edit its output.

Paths you may read: ${cfgFile}, triage/, and /tmp/triage-${RR}/. Do not open, list, search, or print anything under ${FORBIDDEN.join(', ')}. Those paths hold the answer key and the predictions. A read there voids your trials.

Steps:
1. Write the ticket text below, exactly as given, to ${ticketFile}.
2. Run this command once for each trial number in [${ns.join(', ')}]. Each run is a fresh triage session.
   ${RUN_CMD} --config ${cfgFile} --ticket ${ticketFile} --json
3. Each run prints one JSON object. Copy label.category, label.priority, and reply into your result verbatim. Copy runtime, tool call count, tool error count, input tokens, output tokens, and cost into metrics.
4. If a run hits a rate limit, retry it once. If it fails again, set status "rate_limited". If the command crashes or prints invalid JSON, set status "harness_error" and put the first 300 characters of its stderr in error. These are harness outcomes, not model failures. Never retry more than once.
5. List every path you read, listed, or searched in paths_read. Include paths touched by cat, ls, grep, rg, or find.

Ticket ${cell.task.id}:
<<<TICKET
${cell.task.text}
TICKET>>>`;
}

function gradePrompt(cell, todo) {
  const file = `${OUT}/preds/${cell.cfg}/${cell.task.id}.jsonl`;
  const lines = todo
    .map((t) => JSON.stringify({ task_id: cell.task.id, config: cell.cfg, n: t.n, label: t.label ?? null }))
    .join('\n');
  return `You run the code grader. You do not grade anything yourself.

1. Write these ${todo.length} JSON lines to ${file}, one per line, unchanged:
${lines}
2. Run: python ${GRADER} --answers ${ANSWERS} --preds ${file} --json
3. Return grade.py's result for each line as n, category_ok, and priority_ok. Copy its values exactly. Do not reinterpret, fix, or round them.
4. If grade.py exits nonzero, prints invalid JSON, or returns a number of results other than ${todo.length}, set grader_error to the first 300 characters of its output and return an empty grades list.`;
}

function judgePrompt(cell, todo) {
  const replies = todo
    .map((t, i) => `Reply ${i + 1}:\n<<<REPLY\n${t.reply ?? ''}\nREPLY>>>`)
    .join('\n\n');
  return `You judge the tone of first replies to a support ticket. Read ${JUDGE_RUBRIC} and apply its rubric and its pass line exactly. Do not read anything else under spe/. You score tone only. Category and priority are graded elsewhere.

Ticket:
<<<TICKET
${cell.task.text}
TICKET>>>

${replies}

Return one entry per reply with its reply number, the rubric score, pass set by the rubric's pass line, and a one-sentence reason that quotes the reply.`;
}

// ---- Stages ----
async function runTrials(cell, ns, phaseName) {
  if (HALT) return cell;
  const est = EST_TRIAL * ns.length + EST_AGENT;
  if (!reserve(est, `${phaseName} ${cell.key} x${ns.length}`)) return cell;
  let got = [];
  let threw = false;
  try {
    const res = await agent(trialPrompt(cell, ns), {
      label: `${phaseName} ${cell.key}`,
      phase: phaseName,
      schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
      model: HARNESS_MODEL,
    });
    got = (res?.trials ?? []).filter((t) => ns.includes(t.n));
  } catch (e) {
    threw = true;
    log(`${cell.key}: driver failed: ${String(e).slice(0, 200)}`);
  }
  if (threw) {
    settle(est, est);
  } else {
    settle(est, sum(got.map((t) => (isNum(t.metrics?.cost_usd) ? t.metrics.cost_usd : EST_TRIAL))) + EST_AGENT);
  }
  for (const n of ns) {
    const t = got.find((x) => x.n === n) ?? { n, status: 'harness_error', error: 'driver returned no result', paths_read: [] };
    const bad = (t.paths_read ?? []).filter((p) => FORBIDDEN.some((f) => p.includes(f)));
    if (bad.length > 0) {
      t.status = 'void_peeked';
      halt(`${cell.key} trial ${n} read ${bad.join(', ')}. The answer key is reachable from trials.`);
    }
    cell.trials.push(t);
  }
  return cell;
}

async function gradeCell(cell, ns) {
  if (HALT) return cell;
  const todo = cell.trials.filter((t) => ns.includes(t.n) && t.status === 'completed');
  if (todo.length === 0) return cell;
  if (!reserve(EST_AGENT, `Grade ${cell.key}`)) return cell;
  const res = await agent(gradePrompt(cell, todo), {
    label: `Grade ${cell.key}`,
    phase: 'Grade',
    schema: GRADE_SCHEMA,
    model: HARNESS_MODEL,
  });
  const grades = res?.grades ?? [];
  const wantNs = todo.map((t) => t.n).sort().join(',');
  const gotNs = grades.map((g) => g.n).sort().join(',');
  if (res?.grader_error || wantNs !== gotNs) {
    halt(`grader broke on ${cell.key}: ${res?.grader_error ?? `expected trials ${wantNs}, got ${gotNs}`}`);
    return cell;
  }
  for (const g of grades) cell.grades.push({ ...g, pass: g.category_ok && g.priority_ok });
  return cell;
}

async function judgeCell(cell, ns) {
  if (HALT) return cell;
  const todo = cell.trials.filter((t) => ns.includes(t.n) && t.status === 'completed');
  if (todo.length === 0) return cell;
  if (!reserve(EST_JUDGE, `Judge ${cell.key}`)) return cell;
  const res = await agent(judgePrompt(cell, todo), {
    label: `Judge ${cell.key}`,
    phase: 'Judge',
    schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA,
    model: JUDGE_MODEL,
  });
  let mapped = 0;
  for (const s of res?.scores ?? []) {
    const t = todo[s.reply - 1];
    if (t && !cell.judgments.some((j) => j.n === t.n)) {
      cell.judgments.push({ n: t.n, score: s.score, pass: s.pass, reason: s.reason });
      mapped += 1;
    }
  }
  if (mapped !== todo.length) log(`${cell.key}: judge returned ${mapped} of ${todo.length} scores`);
  return cell;
}

// ---- Trials, Grade, Judge ----
phase('Trials');
const first = range(1, TRIALS);
await pipeline(
  cells,
  (c) => runTrials(c, first, 'Trials'),
  (c) => gradeCell(c, first),
  (c) => judgeCell(c, first),
);

// ---- Top-up ----
phase('Top-up');
function cellStats(c) {
  return { graded: c.grades.length, passes: c.grades.filter((g) => g.pass).length };
}
if (!HALT) {
  const mixed = cells
    .map((c) => ({ c, s: cellStats(c) }))
    .filter(({ s }) => s.passes > 0 && s.passes < s.graded)
    .sort((x, y) => Math.abs(x.s.passes / x.s.graded - 0.5) - Math.abs(y.s.passes / y.s.graded - 0.5))
    .map(({ c }) => c);
  const chosen = mixed.slice(0, TOPUP_MAX_CELLS);
  for (const c of mixed.slice(TOPUP_MAX_CELLS)) {
    skipped.push({ what: `Top-up ${c.key}`, reason: `top-up cap of ${TOPUP_MAX_CELLS} cells` });
  }
  log(`Top-up: ${mixed.length} mixed cells, ${chosen.length} topped up by ${TOPUP_PER_CELL} trials each`);
  const extra = range(TRIALS + 1, TOPUP_PER_CELL);
  await pipeline(
    chosen,
    (c) => runTrials(c, extra, 'Top-up'),
    (c) => gradeCell(c, extra),
    (c) => judgeCell(c, extra),
  );
}

// ---- Aggregate ----
function aggregate(cfg, maxN) {
  const cs = cells.filter((c) => c.cfg === cfg);
  const trials = cs.flatMap((c) => c.trials.filter((t) => t.n <= maxN));
  const done = trials.filter((t) => t.status === 'completed');
  const grades = cs.flatMap((c) => c.grades.filter((g) => g.n <= maxN));
  const judged = cs.flatMap((c) => c.judgments.filter((j) => j.n <= maxN));
  const rate = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? round3(xs.filter(f).length / xs.length) : null);
  const calls = sum(done.map((t) => t.metrics?.tool_calls));
  return {
    config: cfg,
    cells: cs.length,
    trials_completed: done.length,
    harness_errors: trials.filter((t) => t.status === 'harness_error').length,
    rate_limited: trials.filter((t) => t.status === 'rate_limited').length,
    voided: trials.filter((t) => t.status === 'void_peeked').length,
    graded: grades.length,
    category_acc: rate(grades, (g) => g.category_ok),
    priority_acc: rate(grades, (g) => g.priority_ok),
    label_acc: rate(grades, (g) => g.pass),
    tone_pass_rate: rate(judged, (j) => j.pass),
    tone_mean_score: mean(judged.map((j) => j.score)),
    mean_runtime_s: mean(done.map((t) => t.metrics?.runtime_s)),
    mean_tool_calls: mean(done.map((t) => t.metrics?.tool_calls)),
    mean_tokens: mean(done.map((t) => (t.metrics ? t.metrics.input_tokens + t.metrics.output_tokens : null))),
    tool_error_rate: calls > 0 ? round3(sum(done.map((t) => t.metrics?.tool_errors)) / calls) : null,
    cost_usd: round2(sum(done.map((t) => t.metrics?.cost_usd))),
  };
}
const primary = Object.keys(CONFIGS).map((cfg) => aggregate(cfg, TRIALS));
const withTopup = Object.keys(CONFIGS).map((cfg) => aggregate(cfg, Infinity));
const SCORED = ['category_acc', 'priority_acc', 'label_acc', 'tone_pass_rate'];
const ceilings = SCORED.filter((m) => primary.every((p) => p[m] === 1));
const shortCells = cells
  .map((c) => ({ cell: c.key, completed: c.trials.filter((t) => t.n <= TRIALS && t.status === 'completed').length }))
  .filter((x) => x.completed < TRIALS);
log(`Spend so far $${round2(spent)} of $${CAP}. ${skipped.length} items skipped. ${shortCells.length} cells short of ${TRIALS} completed trials.`);

// ---- Synthesis ----
phase('Synthesis');
let analysis = null;
let critique = null;
if (HALT) {
  log(`Synthesis skipped because the run halted: ${HALT}`);
} else {
  const failing = cells
    .filter((c) => c.grades.some((g) => !g.pass) || c.judgments.some((j) => !j.pass))
    .slice(0, 60)
    .map((c) => ({
      cell: c.key,
      trials: c.trials
        .filter((t) => t.status === 'completed')
        .map((t) => ({
          n: t.n,
          label: t.label ?? null,
          grade: c.grades.find((g) => g.n === t.n) ?? null,
          tone: c.judgments.find((j) => j.n === t.n) ?? null,
        })),
    }));

  if (reserve(EST_JUDGE, 'Failure analysis')) {
    analysis = await agent(
      `You analyze the eval results of SPE ${RR} for the triage agent. Read ${PREDICTIONS}. Do not edit it or any other file.

For every metric and config in that file, compare the predicted value and band to the measured value in "primary". Primary covers the first ${TRIALS} trials per cell, which is what the predictions were made on. The verdict is "hit" if the measured value falls inside the band and "miss" if it falls outside. Every metric listed in "ceilings" hit the maximum in all configs. Mark those not_scorable and log the saturation as a failure.

Then name the failures. Give each one an ID of the form "${RR} F<number>", a one-line summary, and evidence that names cells and trial numbers. You may read ${ANSWERS} to see the reference labels for failing cells. Harness errors, rate limits, and skipped work are not model failures. List them as harness failures only if they lost data.

Last, propose changes for the next round. Each proposal names the failure ID it comes from. If any metric saturated, propose harder tasks.

Data:
${JSON.stringify({ primary, with_topup: withTopup, ceilings, short_cells: shortCells, failing_cells: failing, skipped, judge_note: JUDGE_NOTE })}`,
      { label: 'Failure analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: ANALYSIS_SCHEMA, model: HARNESS_MODEL },
    );
  }

  if (reserve(EST_JUDGE, 'Completeness critic')) {
    critique = await agent(
      `You are the completeness critic for SPE ${RR}. Check the run below for gaps. Do not edit files.

Check each of these:
- Every cell has ${TRIALS} completed trials, or its gap is explained in short_cells or skipped.
- Every metric and config in ${PREDICTIONS} has a verdict in the analysis.
- Harness errors and rate limits are not counted as model failures.
- The judge note is recorded.
- Skipped work and the top-up cap are listed.
- Failure IDs are unique and each one has evidence.
- Each proposal names a source.
Also state that the transcript scan for reads of spe/evals/ and spe/predictions/ still has to run after this workflow, because paths_read is self-reported.
Return complete as true only if no gaps remain.

Data:
${JSON.stringify({ cells: cells.length, trials_per_cell: TRIALS, primary, short_cells: shortCells, skipped, ceilings, analysis, judge_note: JUDGE_NOTE })}`,
      { label: 'Completeness critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: HARNESS_MODEL },
    );
  }
}

return {
  round: ROUND,
  halted: HALT,
  spend_usd: round2(spent),
  cap_usd: CAP,
  skipped,
  ceilings,
  short_cells: shortCells,
  primary,
  with_topup: withTopup,
  analysis,
  critique,
  judge_note: JUDGE_NOTE,
  cells: cells.map((c) => ({ key: c.key, trials: c.trials, grades: c.grades, judgments: c.judgments })),
};
```
